-- Delaware General Corporation Law (8 Del. C. ch. 1), section 219: list of stockholders entitled to vote; penalty for refusal to
-- produce; stock ledger. Layer 1, from the text alone. Quote lines are copied from de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt by script.
-- Whether the section applies to the kind of corporation is `s 219 the section applies to the kind of corporation` in
-- dg4-s215-nonstock-members.l4 (s 114(b)(2): not read for members, so a stock corporation only).
-- The "penalty" of the heading is the Court's power in (b) to order examination and to postpone the meeting or void its results.

§ `s 219 List of stockholders entitled to vote; penalty for refusal to produce; stock ledger`

§§ `s 219(a) The list`

-- The corporation shall prepare, no later than the tenth day before each meeting of stockholders, a complete list of the
-- stockholders entitled to vote at the meeting; if the record date for determining who may vote is less than 10 days before the
-- meeting date, the list shall reflect the stockholders entitled to vote as of the tenth day before the meeting date.
-- src:836 | The corporation shall prepare, no later than the tenth day before each meeting of stockholders, a complete list of the stockholders entitled to vote at the meeting; provided, however, if the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote is less than 10 days before the meeting date, the list shall reflect the stockholders entitled to vote as of the tenth day before the meeting date, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(a) (src:836)
GIVEN `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 219(a) the last day by which the corporation must prepare the list` `the day of the meeting` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 10) `before` `the day of the meeting`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(a) (src:836)
GIVEN `the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 219(a) the day as of which the list reflects the stockholders entitled to vote` `the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote` `the day of the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote` GREATER THAN (`the date` (`period in days` 10) `before` `the day of the meeting`)
    THEN `the date` (`period in days` 10) `before` `the day of the meeting`
    ELSE `the record date for determining the stockholders entitled to vote`

-- The list is arranged in alphabetical order and shows the address of each stockholder and the number of shares registered in
-- the name of each. Nothing in the section requires the corporation to include electronic mail addresses or other electronic
-- contact information.
-- src:836 | arranged in alphabetical order, and showing the address of each stockholder and the number of shares registered in the name of each stockholder. Nothing contained in this section shall require the corporation to include electronic mail addresses or other electronic contact information on such list. Such list shall be open to the examination of any stockholder for any purpose germane to the meeting for a period of 10 days ending on the day before the meeting date: (i) on a reasonably accessible electronic network, provided that the information required to gain access to such list is provided with the notice of the meeting, or (ii) during ordinary business hours, at the principal place of business of the corporation. In the event that the corporation determines to make the list available on an electronic network, the corporation may take reasonable steps to ensure that such information is available only to stockholders of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(a) (src:836)
GIVEN `the list is arranged in alphabetical order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list shows the address of each stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list shows the number of shares registered in the name of each stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219(a) the list contains what the subsection requires` `the list is arranged in alphabetical order` `the list shows the address of each stockholder` `the list shows the number of shares registered in the name of each stockholder` MEANS
        `the list is arranged in alphabetical order`
    AND `the list shows the address of each stockholder`
    AND `the list shows the number of shares registered in the name of each stockholder`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(a) (src:836)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219(a) the list must include electronic mail addresses or other electronic contact information` MEANS
    FALSE

-- The list shall be open to the examination of any stockholder for any purpose germane to the meeting for a period of 10 days
-- ending on the day before the meeting date: (i) on a reasonably accessible electronic network, provided the information
-- required to gain access is provided with the notice of the meeting, or (ii) during ordinary business hours at the
-- principal place of business of the corporation. The 10 days are the 10th day before the meeting through the day before it.
-- The text says nothing of the meeting day itself (a finding recorded in NOTES.md).
-- src:836 | Such list shall be open to the examination of any stockholder for any purpose germane to the meeting for a period of 10 days ending on the day before the meeting date: (i) on a reasonably accessible electronic network, provided that the information required to gain access to such list is provided with the notice of the meeting, or (ii) during ordinary business hours, at the principal place of business of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(a) (src:836)
GIVEN `the person is a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is germane to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person asks to examine the list` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the list is available on a reasonably accessible electronic network, with the information required to gain access provided with the notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the list is available during ordinary business hours at the principal place of business of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219(a) the stockholder may examine the list` `the person is a stockholder` `the purpose is germane to the meeting` `the day the person asks to examine the list` `the day of the meeting` `the list is available on a reasonably accessible electronic network, with the information required to gain access provided with the notice of the meeting` `the list is available during ordinary business hours at the principal place of business of the corporation` MEANS
        `the person is a stockholder`
    AND `the purpose is germane to the meeting`
    AND `the day the person asks to examine the list` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in days` 10) `before` `the day of the meeting`)
    AND `the day the person asks to examine the list` AT MOST (`the day of the meeting` MINUS 1)
    AND (   `the list is available on a reasonably accessible electronic network, with the information required to gain access provided with the notice of the meeting`
         OR `the list is available during ordinary business hours at the principal place of business of the corporation`)

-- If the corporation determines to make the list available on an electronic network, it may take reasonable steps to ensure
-- that the information is available only to stockholders.
-- src:836 | In the event that the corporation determines to make the list available on an electronic network, the corporation may take reasonable steps to ensure that such information is available only to stockholders of the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(a) (src:836)
GIVEN `the corporation makes the list available on an electronic network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219(a) the corporation may take reasonable steps to ensure the information is available only to stockholders` `the corporation makes the list available on an electronic network` MEANS
    `the corporation makes the list available on an electronic network`

§§ `s 219(b) Refusal to permit examination`

-- If the corporation, or an officer or agent of the corporation, refuses to permit examination of the list by a stockholder, the
-- stockholder may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel the examination.
-- src:837 | If the corporation, or an officer or agent of the corporation, refuses to permit examination of the list by a stockholder, such stockholder may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel the corporation to permit such examination. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(b) (src:837)
GIVEN `the person is a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation, or an officer or agent of the corporation, refuses to permit the person to examine the list` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219(b) the stockholder may apply to the Court of Chancery for an order to compel the corporation to permit the examination` `the person is a stockholder` `the corporation, or an officer or agent of the corporation, refuses to permit the person to examine the list` MEANS
        `the person is a stockholder`
    AND `the corporation, or an officer or agent of the corporation, refuses to permit the person to examine the list`

-- The burden of proof is on the corporation to establish that the examination the stockholder seeks is for a purpose not germane
-- to the meeting.
-- src:837 | The burden of proof shall be on the corporation to establish that the examination such stockholder seeks is for a purpose not germane to the meeting. The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit examination of the list upon such conditions as the Court may deem appropriate, and may make such additional orders as may be appropriate, including, without limitation, postponing the meeting or voiding the results of the meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(b) (src:837)
GIVETH A `Actor`
`s 219(b) the party who bears the burden of proof that the examination sought is for a purpose not germane to the meeting` MEANS
    `the corporation`

-- The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit examination upon such conditions as it deems appropriate, and may make
-- such additional orders as may be appropriate, including, without limitation, postponing the meeting or voiding the results.
-- src:837 | The Court may summarily order the corporation to permit examination of the list upon such conditions as the Court may deem appropriate, and may make such additional orders as may be appropriate, including, without limitation, postponing the meeting or voiding the results of the meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(b) (src:837)
DECLARE `s 219(b) Order the Court may make` IS ONE OF
    `a summary order that the corporation permit examination of the list upon such conditions as the Court deems appropriate`
    `an additional order postponing the meeting`
    `an additional order voiding the results of the meeting`
    `any other additional order that is appropriate`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(b) (src:837)
GIVEN order IS A `s 219(b) Order the Court may make`
      `a stockholder has applied for an order under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219(b) the Court of Chancery may make the order` order `a stockholder has applied for an order under this subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `a summary order that the corporation permit examination of the list upon such conditions as the Court deems appropriate` THEN `a stockholder has applied for an order under this subsection`
    WHEN `an additional order postponing the meeting` THEN `a stockholder has applied for an order under this subsection`
    WHEN `an additional order voiding the results of the meeting` THEN `a stockholder has applied for an order under this subsection`
    WHEN `any other additional order that is appropriate` THEN `a stockholder has applied for an order under this subsection`

§§ `s 219(c) The stock ledger`

-- For purposes of this chapter, "stock ledger" means 1 or more records administered by or on behalf of the corporation in which
-- the names of all of the corporation's stockholders of record, the address and number of shares registered in the name of
-- each, and all issuances and transfers of stock of the corporation are recorded in accordance with s 224.
-- src:838 | For purposes of this chapter, “stock ledger” means 1 or more records administered by or on behalf of the corporation in which the names of all of the corporation’s stockholders of record, the address and number of shares registered in the name of each such stockholder, and all issuances and transfers of stock of the corporation are recorded in accordance with § 224 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(c) (src:838)
GIVEN `the records are administered by or on behalf of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the names of all of the corporation's stockholders of record are recorded in them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address and number of shares registered in the name of each stockholder are recorded in them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all issuances and transfers of stock of the corporation are recorded in them in accordance with s 224` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: s 224 (piece dg5)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219(c) the records are the stock ledger` `the records are administered by or on behalf of the corporation` `the names of all of the corporation's stockholders of record are recorded in them` `the address and number of shares registered in the name of each stockholder are recorded in them` `all issuances and transfers of stock of the corporation are recorded in them in accordance with s 224` MEANS
        `the records are administered by or on behalf of the corporation`
    AND `the names of all of the corporation's stockholders of record are recorded in them`
    AND `the address and number of shares registered in the name of each stockholder are recorded in them`
    AND `all issuances and transfers of stock of the corporation are recorded in them in accordance with s 224`

-- The stock ledger is the only evidence as to who are the stockholders entitled by this section to examine the list or to vote
-- in person or by proxy at any meeting of stockholders. So a person is shown to be entitled only if the ledger shows the person
-- to be a stockholder of record.
-- src:838 | The stock ledger shall be the only evidence as to who are the stockholders entitled by this section to examine the list required by this section or to vote in person or by proxy at any meeting of stockholders.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 219(c) (src:838)
GIVEN `the stock ledger shows the person as a stockholder of record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 219(c) the stock ledger shows the person to be a stockholder entitled to examine the list or to vote` `the stock ledger shows the person as a stockholder of record` MEANS
    `the stock ledger shows the person as a stockholder of record`
